+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** The frai-core test suite has two failing tests: governance tests fail because `APPROVAL_STATUSES` is not exported as a named export, and evaluation tests fail because the toxicity metric receives references as banned terms instead of default banned terms.
+
+**Approach:** Export `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from the governance module, and wrap the toxicityMetric in DEFAULT_METRICS to prevent references from being passed as banned terms.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:** Keep all existing public exports working. Do not edit, skip, or delete any test files. Ensure all 28 tests pass.
+
+**Never:** Do not modify test files or remove any public APIs.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| Governance validation error message | Invalid approval status | Error message includes comma-separated list of valid statuses | APPROVAL_STATUSES must be exported |
+| Default evaluations run | outputs and references arrays | toxicity score of 1 for safe content | toxicityMetric must only receive outputs |
+| Exact match evaluation | matching outputs and references | score of 1 | Score calculated correctly |
+
+</intent-contract>
+
